(740, 'woocommerce_admin_notice_php81_required_in_woo_116', '<div class=\"wc-php-version-notice\"><h4>PHP version requirements will change soon</h4><p>WooCommerce 11.6, planned for release in <b>February 2027</b>, will require PHP 8.1 or newer to work. Your server is currently running PHP 8.0.30, so this change will impact your store. Please contact your hosting provider to upgrade to the latest PHP 8.3 release or newer (PHP 8.1 is the minimum WooCommerce will require).</p>\n<p><b>Your PHP version may also be affected by critical security vulnerabilities.</b> Official PHP 8.0.30 releases do not include the fixes for CVE-2026-109618 and CVE-2026-109619 (disclosed in October 2026), which can let attackers run code on your server. Some hosting providers apply these fixes themselves, so when you contact yours about upgrading, ask them to confirm your server is patched.</p>\n<p class=\"wc-php-version-notice__learn-more\"><b><a href=\"https://developer.woocommerce.com/2026/09/29/php-8-1-requirement/?utm_source=admin_notice&amp;utm_medium=product&amp;utm_campaign=php81_requirement&amp;utm_content=learn_more\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more about this change<span class=\"screen-reader-text\"> (opens in a new tab)</span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"dashicons dashicons-external\"></span></a></b></p></div>', 'auto'),
